<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 415 0 R/Alt(Post-training mean excitatory rate (black diamonds, left axis) and test accuracy (red squares, right axis) against integration timestep on a logarithmic abscissa spanning 0.05 to 1.0 ms. The excitatory rate stays within a narrow low band and is non-monotonic in the timestep, so finer stepping does not buy a lower rate; accuracy stays essentially flat across the range. Both training and inference use the same timestep at each point.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[0]/Pg 1288 0 R>>
